-- title:
--   Each call only requires the low bank to be small.
-- statement:
--   Each call only requires the low bank to be small. Previously cached high
--   registers keep their previous size bound, so the caller can reuse the same polynomial
--   encoding bound across arbitrarily many calls.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.MinorProxyCache.rational_nativeSafe`.
